AB  - Geospatial data science offers significant insights derived from spatial information. It is employed to examine various locations within urban areas, facilitating advancements in transportation, healthcare, disaster management, and urban planning. Geospatial information encompasses both spatial and temporal data obtained from satellite imagery and street view images. A diverse array of spatial data can be input into the system to identify valuable patterns. This research study presents a comprehensive review of geospatial data science, detailing its methodologies and applications. Image processing serves as a crucial technique for segmenting regions within satellite images. Additionally, deep learning algorithms are utilized to develop models that analyze the data, yielding efficient information. © 2025 IEEE.
