AB  - Urban renewal in aging residential areas is a key challenge for sustainable city development since inefficient area identification for intervention can lead to resource misallocation and urban deterioration. Present research proposes an automated framework based on remote sensing information and GeoAI technologies for effective identification of potential renewal areas. Satellite high-resolution imagery and geospatial information are used for extracting critical urban features such as building density, land use intensity, and structural status. XGBoost, LightGBM, and Decision Tree are used for machine learning classification and prioritization based on renewal urgency while ESRGAN-aided images refine feature extraction quality. Its novelty is based on an integration of GeoAI with super-resolution imaging as well as state-of-the-art machine learning classifiers for effective spatial pattern discovery as well as predictive analysis such that detection performance is enhanced significantly. Testing in a metropolitan residential area indicated a detection accuracy above 95% for renewal area detection. Proposed is a framework for enabling urban planners with information- driven decision-making capabilities for sustainable urbanization. ©2026 IEEE.
