AB  - The ecosystem services (ES) framework is an emerging topic addressing the issue of promoting sustainability in planning. One of its strengths is its ability to facilitate spatially explicit assessments, which can help elicit conflicts between human and nature in a functional perspective. This study aimed to exploit the informative potential of the ES framework to produce new geographies of the territory based on a formal and quantitative assessment of different levels and categories of territorial specialization in ES provisioning, using innovative geoAI techniques. The research was based on previous studies where ES supply had been computed at the national level and tested on a sample area. The study area included several environmental challenges, socio-economic underdevelopment, and potentials in the tourism sector. The paper discusses how the integration of ES with machine learning techniques enhances the informative potential in spatial explicit classification of a study area. The results show a high degree of spatial interpretation potential derived from the regionalization map in terms of statistical similarity of detected regions. The study concludes by highlighting the need to better define the concept of territorial specialization in ES provisioning to reinforce the methodological proposal extending to other relevant case studies. © 2023, The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG.
