AB  - The urban organism has become very complex as its planning and management have become a hydra-headed problem in Africa due to rapid population growth and inadequate technological expertise. Population in African cities is projected to increase significantly by 2050, requiring smart tools, namely artificial intelligence (AI) and geographic AI (Geo-AI), to manage the cities to accommodate the expected population increase. This chapter discussed the application of AI and Geo-AI in urban planning and management in Africa to understand the extent of its application and how it can be used to lessen population pressure on African cities. Documentary analysis was used to assess the contents of literature in the areas of global perspective and advances of Geo-AI in urban planning, applications of Geo-AI in urban planning and management in Africa, and opportunities and challenges of Geo-AI. The application of Geo-AI is widespread in the Global North but limited in the Global South. Geo-AI has promising economic potential and would propel urban planning in the Global South if regional and sub-regional bodies such as the African Union and Economic Community of West African States would establish regional and sub-regional AI and Geo-AI infrastructure, such as data houses, internet, and capacity building centres. © 2025 selection and editorial matter, Abubakari Ahmed, Millicent A. Akaateba, and Bernard A. A. Akanbang; individual chapters, the contributors. All rights reserved.
